Niki Agent
==========

Niki Agent is a presentation-layer fork of Deep Agents.

This product includes software developed by LangChain, Inc.
(https://www.langchain.com/), specifically the `deepagents-code` package from
the Deep Agents project (https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents).

Upstream copyright and license notices are retained verbatim:

    MIT License
    Copyright (c) LangChain, Inc.

The full license text is preserved at the repository root in `LICENSE`, and at
`libs/code/LICENSE` for the package this fork is derived from. Those files are
unchanged from upstream.

What Niki changes
-----------------

Niki changes presentation and responsiveness only:

  * Product naming and a new `niki` console script. The `dcode` and
    `deepagents-code` commands are unchanged and still work.
  * A Niki theme, registered through upstream's existing theme registry.
  * Responsiveness defaults: a bounded mounted-message window and a
    non-blinking composer cursor by default.
  * An outbound-network policy that defaults update checking, auto-update, and
    remote managed-config fetching to off. See `docs/niki/DESIGN.md` §5.

What Niki does NOT change
-------------------------

  * The `libs/deepagents` SDK package. It is not modified; the diff against the
    fork point is empty and must remain so.
  * Agent behaviour, the tool set, the permission defaults, or approval
    semantics. Approvals remain as upstream ships them.
  * Configuration, session, or history storage paths (`~/.deepagents/`), and
    environment variable names.

Third-party components
----------------------

Niki depends on the same third-party packages as upstream, including Textual,
Rich, LangChain, and LangGraph. Their licenses apply unchanged; see
`libs/code/pyproject.toml` for the dependency list.